              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioner argues that the Court of Appeals erred in dismissing its improper fact\u2011finding claim."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1c0b8504ef7b5036a3e37a2b0e987a2703a806724dd38aae6e2e02e4095425cd",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1c0b8504ef7b-0003-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 75,
                "start": 75
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the phrase \u201cas of right\u201d in \u00a71252(d)(1) has a specific purpose and only the petitioner can give it meaning."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1c0b8504ef7b5036a3e37a2b0e987a2703a806724dd38aae6e2e02e4095425cd",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1c0b8504ef7b-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 66,
                "start": 66
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, an impermissible fact\u2011finding claim occurs when the Board relies on facts the immigration judge did not consider."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "523f28ee5dcc03b08320fba42182bda07a87c6300af4eca30f8ded2febcc96ea",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-523f28ee5dcc-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 11,
                "start": 11
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The Government contends that \u00a71252(d)(1) is jurisdictional because it addresses the court and limits review."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1c0b8504ef7b5036a3e37a2b0e987a2703a806724dd38aae6e2e02e4095425cd",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1c0b8504ef7b-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Government, the Government acknowledges that waiver and forfeiture apply to \u00a71252(d)(1)."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "523f28ee5dcc03b08320fba42182bda07a87c6300af4eca30f8ded2febcc96ea",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-523f28ee5dcc-0001-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 16,
                "start": 16
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Government, the exhaustion requirement only demands exhaustion of remedies \u201cavailable as of right,\u201d not discretionary remedies."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1c0b8504ef7b5036a3e37a2b0e987a2703a806724dd38aae6e2e02e4095425cd",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1c0b8504ef7b-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The Government argues that the statute requires filing a petition for review and, simultaneously, a motion to reconsider before the Board."
        }
      ],
